### Figure 2 — as printed in the paper

Figure 2. Vector field results from different coupling strate- gies. Random coupling forces the model to regress inconsistent (gray) velocity targets, creating ambiguous intersections and push- ing the model toward an averaged (purple) direction, which pro- duces curved velocity fields. In contrast, optimal transport provides consistent couplings with fewer intersections, enabling the model to learn much straighter velocity fields.

